  "worked_solution": "A partition of a set $X$ is a collection of non-empty subsets of $X$ where every element of $X$ is contained in *exactly* one subset. \n\nOf the given collections, only ${{f,g,h},{i},{j,k,l}}$ is a partition.\n\nThe rest of the collections are not partitions:\n\n- ${∅,{f,g,h,i},{j,k,l}}$ is not a partition because the subset $∅$ is empty.\n\n- ${∅,{f},{g,h,i},{j,k,l}}$ is not a partition because the subset $∅$ is empty.\n\n- ${{f,g,h},{h,i},{h,j,f,k,l}}$ is not a partition because the elements $f$ and $h$ appear in multiple subsets.\n\n- ${{f,g,h},{k,l}}$ is not a partition because the elements $i,j\\in X$ do not appear in any subset.",
